\section{Traits}{

The trait table covers 30,938 species of ray-finned fishes. Morphological,
ecological and life-history traits come from FishBase; entries missing there
were completed by iterative conditional imputation, so every species carries
a complete predictor vector. Traits whose imputation could not be validated
accurately enough were excluded from the model and are not part of this
table.
}

\section{Phylogeny}{

Relatedness enters as twenty phylogenetic eigenvectors, obtained from a
truncated singular value decomposition of the tip-by-ancestral-node
incidence matrix of the fully sampled ray-finned fish phylogeny of the Fish
Tree of Life (Rabosky et al. 2018), in the version in which species without
molecular data are grafted within their taxonomic group by the TACT procedure
of Chang et al. (2020). Species absent from that phylogeny are absent from
this table as well, since they cannot be described by these predictors.
}

\section{Model}{

The forest is an ensemble of 100 replicas of 10 trees. Every replica was
fitted to all documented interactions and to an equal-sized independent draw
from the pseudo-absence pool, and the predicted score is the average over
replicas. Documented interactions come from the Global Biotic Interactions
database; pseudo-absences are pairs of species that are recorded together in
the same biogeographic province within the same decade and that the database
does not report as interacting.
}

